  {
    "sha": "43b789ed81326f8485e1b63f5cf69126d0a67b57",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKDQzYjc4OWVkODEzMjZmODQ4NWUxYjYzZjVjZjY5MTI2ZDBhNjdiNTc",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-17T10:14:54Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-17T10:14:54Z"
      },
      "message": "perf(ui): read the generation label from the entity, with no doc_version key\n\n4ac78101 stored the label and resolved it again when doc_version\nchanged. The #2238 frame-cost rule does not permit a cache key on\ndoc_version alone. The job now finds its operation entity one time,\nwhen it starts. Each frame reads the label from that entity through the\nnew model::live_operation_label, which checks World::is_alive first. A\nrename shows at once, and a deleted operation shows its name.\n\nPinned by one_search_for_each_job_and_a_rename_shows_without_another and\na_deleted_operation_shows_its_name_and_no_dead_entity_is_read.\n\nRefs #2257\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
